<LegalPage
  title="Privacy"
  description="What cello.design and Cello's personal tools collect, and what they don't."
  canonicalPath="/privacy/"
  updated="November 7, 2026"
>
  <p>
    This page covers this website, cello.design, and channel-hub, a private tool I built to read analytics from my
    own YouTube, Instagram, TikTok and Twitch accounts. It's written in plain language because there isn't much to say.
  </p>

  <h2>This website</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>No ads and no tracking cookies.</li>
    <li>
      Right now there are no analytics. I plan to add PostHog soon to count page views and clicks on links and buttons. It
      will run cookieless, with no session recording and without capturing anything you type. I'll update this page
      when it goes live.
    </li>
    <li>
      Your light or dark theme choice is saved in your own browser's local storage so the site remembers it. It never
      leaves your device.
    </li>
    <li>
      Some posts embed YouTube videos. They use YouTube's privacy-enhanced player (youtube-nocookie.com), and YouTube's
      own privacy policy applies once you press play.
    </li>
    <li>
      The site is hosted on Netlify, which keeps standard server logs (such as IP address and pages requested) to run
      and protect the service. I don't use those logs to identify visitors.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>channel-hub</h2>
  <p>
    channel-hub signs in only to accounts I own, with read-only permissions I approve on each platform's own sign-in
    screen. It isn't offered to anyone else.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>What it reads:</strong> my accounts' public profile details and statistics, such as follower counts,
      and per-post views, likes, comments, shares, saves, watch time and audience retention.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>What it doesn't read:</strong> other people's accounts, private messages, or the text of comments and who wrote them.
      It can't post, edit or delete anything.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Where it lives:</strong> on my own computer and private server. Sign-in tokens are stored in a file only
      I can read. Nothing is sold, shared or used for advertising.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Removing access:</strong> I can revoke it at any time from each platform's connected-apps settings, which
      stops all collection, and I can delete the stored data.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions: <a href="mailto:cello@cello.design">cello@cello.design</a>.</p>
</LegalPage>
